#!/bin/bash
# pwsync/help.loc - Module-specific help

cat <<'EOF'
Module: pwsync - user-driven password propagation across the cluster

  This module ships the unprivileged command users run to change their own
  password everywhere. Root-side account work - creating users and groups,
  setting or resetting a password - lives in the 'accounts' module.

SUBCOMMANDS

  setup                          Install /usr/local/bin/pwsync and
                                 /etc/pwsync.conf on the target host.
      yamc -h HOST -u root pwsync

CLUSTER HELPER  (yamc.local/bin/)

  pwsync-cluster-deploy          Install/update pwsync on every host

END-USER COMMAND  (installed on each host)

  pwsync                         Change your password here and on all peers
  pwsync --local-only            Change it here only

CONFIGURATION

  yamc.local/cluster.conf        CLUSTER_HOSTS - shared with other modules
  yamc.local/pwsync/cluster.conf PWSYNC_HOSTS  - override, only if password
                                 sync needs a different host set

  ~/.pwsync-hosts                Optional per-user host list. Lives in the
                                 user's NFS home so it applies everywhere.
                                 Use it when someone has accounts on only
                                 some hosts, to stop the others being
                                 reported as skipped.

RESULTS

  ok         Password changed there
  skipped    ssh exited 255 - host unreachable, or no account/key there
  FAILED     Reached the host but its passwd refused: genuine drift.
             Repair with:  accounts setpass USERNAME  on that host.
EOF
